  "finalText": "### Summary of Changes\n\nThree targeted source fixes were implemented to restore the documented data contract:\n\n1. **CSV EOF Record Termination (`src/csv.mjs`)**:\n   - In `parseCsv`, committed any in-progress record when reaching end-of-file without a trailing newline (`if (recordStarted || record.length > 0) endRecord();`), ensuring files lacking a trailing newline retain their final record (including trailing empty fields and quoted fields) without generating phantom records.\n\n2. **Half-Cent Decimal Rounding (`src/money.mjs`)**:\n   - In `parseMoney`, replaced floating-point `Math.round(Number(text) * 100)` with exact integer arithmetic (`BigInt`). Decimal strings with up to four fractional digits are scaled to ten-thousandths and rounded half away from zero symmetrically for positive and negative values using `sign * ((tenThousandths + 50n) / 100n)`.\n\n3. **Vendor-Scoped Invoice Identity (`src/dedupe.mjs`)**:\n   - In `invoiceKey`, changed the identity key from `invoice.invoiceId` to `JSON.stringify([invoice.vendorId, invoice.invoiceId])`. This ensures collision safety across arbitrary vendor IDs while scoping invoice IDs by supplier, matching payment routing in `src/payments.mjs`.\n\n### Commands Run and Actual Results\n\n- `node --test test/*.test.mjs`:\n  - Baseline: 38 passed, 6 failed (failing tests in CLI mixed-feed output, CSV EOF termination, vendor invoice identity scoping, money half-cent symmetric rounding, mixed supplier feed import, and supplier payment routing).\n  - Post-fix: 44 passed, 0 failed.\n\n- `node bin/ledger.mjs import data/invoices.csv --payments data/payments.csv --as-of 2026-03-01 --format json`:\n  - Exit code: `0`.\n  - Output verified: all 4 invoices imported across 3 vendors, exact half-cent rounding applied (`1.005` to `1.01` USD, `10.075` to `10.08` USD, `-1.005` to `-1.01` USD), `totalCents: 1208`, 0 diagnostics, and all 3 payments successfully applied to their respective vendor/invoice records.\n\n- `npm test`:\n  - 44 passed, 0 failed.",
